+**Disagree**
+
+IR-001 severity:blocker status:open
+
+The plan-affected exemption lets a tracked outside-scope file pass the
+pre-worker floor, but that same path is then captured in the set-once
+`before_tracked` baseline and excluded from the task commit, producing a stale
+reviewed range on the integrity boundary this family guards.
+
+`_floor_outside_scope` now allows `p in plan_affected`
+(`.redteam/workflows/phase_runners/implement.py:305`). When an outside-scope
+tracked file listed in the approved `outcome.md` Affected files is dirty-vs-base
+BEFORE the first implement round, it is stored in `before_tracked` via the
+set-once tracked baseline. `_commit_worker_diff` then stages only
+`set(_tracked_changed_paths(...)) - before_tracked`
+(`.redteam/workflows/phase_runners/implement.py:437`), so the worker's edits to
+that file are omitted from the WIP commit and from `git diff <base>...HEAD`. The
+post-commit integrity gate does not catch it: `_uncommitted_scope_files` checks
+only source/test roots and `_uncommitted_outside_scope_files` checks only NEW
+untracked outside-scope files — a tracked, already-dirty, outside-scope,
+plan-affected leftover is covered by neither. Verification then runs against a
+worktree that contains the change while the committed diff handed to review
+omits it.
+
+This is exactly the failure mode #137 must not open: the exemption declares
+those outside-scope paths to be task scope, so commit / integrity attribution
+has to account for them. Fix fail-closed so any plan-affected path with changes
+vs base is either committed into the reviewed range or fails the post-commit
+integrity gate (no silent omission), preserving the operator-WIP and
+adversarial-baseline guarantees. Add a regression: an outside-scope
+Affected-files path dirty before the first implement round has the worker's
+change reflected in `base...HEAD` (or the gate refuses).
+
+(Source: cross-model standalone stack review over the combined #141+#142 diff.
+The per-task `review_code` gate saw only `parent...HEAD` and did not exercise
+the commit-attribution interaction; this round carries the finding back into the
+worker+reviewer loop.)
+
+**Agree**
+
+The floor parser, set-once snapshot, `..`/absolute rejection, and the decision
+to keep `_cross_run_trust_root_floor` out of the exemption path are sound and
+should be preserved as-is.
+
+REVIEW_DECISION: CHANGES_REQUESTED
